{
 "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
 "$id": "urn:opensip:m1:native-wire-carriers-input:4",
 "title": "Closed grammar of wire-carriers.v1.json (AUTHOR candidate 04)",
 "description": "Shape of the declarative carrier input only. It proves nothing about CBOR canonicality, NFC, UTF-8 byte bounds, joins or commitments; check.py, admission-vectors.json and handwritten admission own those. `lexical` names a normative handwritten rule; `pattern` follows privateRepresentation.patternDialect. All integer literals are decimal strings. An absent maxItems/maxBytes/maxScalars/maxUtf8Bytes means bounded only by the protocol's maxFramePayloadBytes (admission FRAME-LIMIT).",
 "type": "object",
 "additionalProperties": false,
 "required": [
